# ── Privacy boundary (RISKS P-01, ADR-0007) ─────────────────────────────
# Real career data NEVER enters this public repo. The committed
# docs/profile.example/ (fictional) is used by tests, fixtures, and demos.
docs/profile/

# Secrets — .env.example (documented variable names only) is committed
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local data: database dumps, backups, exports of real postings/applications.
# Dumps of dev contain real profile rows — no dump naming variant may ever be
# commit-eligible. /*.sql only ignores repo-root files (a plain-format pg_dump
# landing there); committed migrations live under packages/db/migrations/.
*.dump
*.backup
*.sql.gz
/*.sql
backups/
exports/
# M13-01: the profile tar + row-count manifest db:backup mints (belt-and-suspenders;
# these live OUTSIDE the repo by enforced check, but never let one become commit-eligible).
# The .age variants are the NC-1(b) cloud branch's encrypted dump + tar.
careerforge-profile-*.tar
careerforge-profile-*.tar.age
careerforge-db-*.manifest.json
careerforge-db-*.dump.age

# ── Dependencies & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
# pnpm store, should it ever land in-repo (the devcontainer pins its store
# to a container path; this is belt-and-suspenders for a public repo).
.pnpm-store/
dist/
# `nuxt generate` drops a convenience symlink `dist -> .output/public` at the
# app root; the `dist/` rule above matches directories only, so name the link.
apps/*/dist
.output/
.nuxt/
.nitro/
# Nuxt Content's build-time SQLite database (regenerated every build).
.data/
coverage/
# Lighthouse CI reports (LHR json/html), regenerated by `pnpm lighthouse` (M2-03).
.lighthouseci/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
# settings.json is deliberately committed: mechanism B (RISKS S-03) hides
# .env from the editor surface and must survive fresh clones.
!.vscode/settings.json

# ── Playwright run artifacts (e2e traces may embed rendered pages) ──────
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ---- Terraform (M10-06): local state + operator tfvars never committed ----
# example.tfvars (fictional, name-only) IS committed; terraform.tfvars (real
# operator values) and ALL state are ignored. State carries no secret (ADR-0022
# D4), so this is a durability concern only. .terraform.lock.hcl is committed
# (reproducible provider pins) and deliberately NOT ignored here.
infra/terraform/.terraform/
infra/terraform/*.tfstate
infra/terraform/*.tfstate.*
infra/terraform/*.tfvars
!infra/terraform/example.tfvars
# Saved plan files (terraform plan -out=...) can embed variable values (M10-08
# finding: a stray `tfplan` was left untracked-but-not-ignored after the go-live
# ceremony). Never commit them.
infra/terraform/tfplan
infra/terraform/*.tfplan

# @nuxt/test-utils writes a version stamp into each app's .nuxtrc on every
# toolchain run; tracking them makes clean trees dirty themselves after any
# test-utils bump (PR#188 drift, notes/nuxtrc-stamp-drift-2026-08-13.md).
# Tool-owned, stamp-only files - untracked by decision.
.nuxtrc

# Shared Claude Code config. Every clone's .git/info/exclude carries a broad
# `.claude/` line - local state that `git clone` never propagates - which made
# new agents/skills invisible to `git status` and reachable only via `git add -f`.
# A tracked negation overrides that. Deny-by-default INSIDE .claude/ so this
# cannot silently start tracking runtime state or personal local files
# (.claude/commands/boot.md is deliberately untracked).
#
# ANCHORING IS LOAD-BEARING, and the first version of this block got it wrong
# in a way that made a PUBLIC repo more exposed than main. `!.claude/` has no
# leading slash, so git matches it at ANY depth and un-ignored every nested
# .claude directory too - while the deny-by-default line that was supposed to
# re-exclude their contents DID contain a slash, so it only ever applied to
# the root one. Net effect: running `claude` from apps/web/ would have put that
# directory's local state in front of `git add -A`. Every rule below is now
# explicitly root-anchored, and the unanchored `.claude/` on the first line
# keeps nested ones ignored without depending on .git/info/exclude, which is
# per-clone state a fresh clone does not have.
#
# THE SHAPE, and why it is this one. Three earlier attempts each failed in a
# different direction, so the reasoning is kept:
#
#   (1) `!/.claude/agents/**` re-included whole subtrees, which cancels EVERY
#       earlier rule in this file for anything under them - `.env`, `*.dump`,
#       `backups/`, `careerforge-profile-*.tar`, the whole privacy-boundary
#       block whose own comment says "no dump naming variant may ever be
#       commit-eligible".
#   (2) Listing the cancelled rules back by hand covered 4 of them.
#   (3) An extension allowlist (`!/.claude/**/*.md`) fixed that and broke the
#       OPPOSITE way: a skill's `scripts/run.sh`, `reference.txt` or
#       `schema.json`, and `.claude/hooks/README.md`, all became invisible to
#       `git add -A` and reachable only through `git add -f` - which is
#       verbatim the trap this whole block exists to remove. It also split
#       macOS from Linux, because `core.ignorecase` made `README.MD` visible
#       here and ignored in CI.
#
# So: re-include the four shared subtrees WHOLE, then re-exclude the categories
# that must never be committed. That tail is a DENYLIST and denylists go stale -
# it is written out rather than pretended away, and its reference list is
# `.claude/hooks/guard-secrets.sh`, which enumerates the same credential
# filenames for the same reason. Add to both together.
.claude/
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/agents/**
!/.claude/skills/
!/.claude/skills/**
!/.claude/rules/
!/.claude/rules/**
!/.claude/hooks/
!/.claude/hooks/**
!/.claude/settings.json

# --- and never these, anywhere under .claude/ ---------------------------------
# Credentials and keys (mirrors .claude/hooks/guard-secrets.sh).
/.claude/**/.env
/.claude/**/.env.*
!/.claude/**/.env.example
/.claude/**/*.env
/.claude/**/.envrc
/.claude/**/.envrc.*
!/.claude/**/.envrc.example
/.claude/**/id_rsa*
/.claude/**/id_dsa*
/.claude/**/id_ecdsa*
/.claude/**/id_ed25519*
/.claude/**/*.pem
/.claude/**/*.key
/.claude/**/*.p12
/.claude/**/*.pfx
/.claude/**/*.jks
/.claude/**/*.p8
/.claude/**/credentials.json
/.claude/**/service-account*.json
/.claude/**/token.json
/.claude/**/.git-credentials
/.claude/**/.npmrc
/.claude/**/.netrc
/.claude/**/.pgpass
/.claude/**/kubeconfig
/.claude/**/secrets.yaml
/.claude/**/secrets.yml
/.claude/**/.htpasswd
/.claude/**/.pypirc
/.claude/**/*.tfvars
# Real data - the privacy boundary at the top of this file, re-stated in scope.
/.claude/**/*.dump
/.claude/**/*.backup
/.claude/**/*.sql
/.claude/**/*.sql.gz
/.claude/**/backups/
/.claude/**/exports/
/.claude/**/careerforge-db-*
/.claude/**/careerforge-profile-*
# Machine noise.
/.claude/**/.DS_Store
/.claude/**/Thumbs.db
/.claude/**/node_modules/
/.claude/**/coverage/
/.claude/**/*.log
/.claude/**/*.tsbuildinfo

